; rhythms.moritz - rhythms and lines, from Musil's algorithmic_comp.mu: three random walks, each
; note within three semitones of the one before (walk); a chord arpeggiated up, down and up a whole
; tone higher each time (arpeggio); a polyrhythm, a notes against b in every two beats on the oboe
; and the horn (polyrhythm of two tuplets); under it a cello ostinato from a pattern
; (rhythm-from-pattern "x..x.x..": x an attack, a dot a continuation), then the same augmented,
; twice as slow (fragment-scale).
; Try: 1. play; 2. another polyrhythm: 4 3, 5 4, 7 4 (the oboe's notes, then the horn's, in every
; two beats); 3. double-click the score box, Roll: the two lines of the polyrhythm one above the
; other, their onsets meeting at every second beat; 4. double-click the code box: another pattern,
; another step for the walks, Cmd-S, then a polyrhythm again.
(patch
  (obj title comment "rhythms: walks, arpeggios, a polyrhythm, an ostinato from a pattern and its augmentation" (pos 20 12))
  (obj sub comment "a polyrhythm writes the score again; play" (pos 20 34))
  (obj dmic message microsol (pos 20 62))
  (obj dful message fullsol (pos 100 62))
  (obj cds comment "the samples: MicroSOL (comes with Moritz: Ob Hn Vn Vc, C4-G4) or FullSOL (registered in Extras > Datasets...); then compose again" (pos 170 63))
  (obj r1 message "3 2" (pos 150 97))
  (obj r2 message "4 3" (pos 195 97))
  (obj r3 message "5 4" (pos 240 97))
  (obj r4 message "7 4" (pos 285 97))
  (obj lb loadbang (pos 340 97))
  (obj cctl comment "a against b" (pos 430 98))
  (obj c code 2 1 (pos 20 132)
    (script
      "; rhythms and lines, from Musil's algorithmic_comp.mu: walks, arpeggios up and down, a polyrhythm, an ostinato from a"
      "; pattern and its augmentation. in1 the polyrhythm (3 2: three against two), in2 the dataset"
      "load \"music.mu\""
      "var name (if (equal? in2 nil) \"microsol\" in2)     ; MicroSOL comes with Moritz: Ob Hn Vn Vc, C4-G4 (a sketch)"
      "var db (db-load name)                             ; fullsol: FullSOL where you registered it (Extras > Datasets...)"
      "var pr-of (if (equal? in1 nil) (list 3 2) (vec->list in1))"
      "seed 6"
      "var s (score \"rhythms\" 44100)"
      "score-tempo! s 108                                  ; the times below in beats (add-beats!)"
      "; 1. three random walks, a step of at most three semitones (0-6 beats)"
      "add-beats! s 0 (walk db (list 'Ob 'Hn 'Vc) 'mf 'ord (list \"A4\" \"D#4\" \"G3\") 3 (rhythm (list 0.5 0.5 0.5 1 0.5 0.5 1)))"
      "; 2. a chord arpeggiated up, down, up, a whole tone higher each time (6-12)"
      "each (list 0 2 4) (function (k) (add-beats! s (+ 6 k) (arpeggio db 'Vn 'p 'ord (transpose-pitches (list \"C4\" \"F#4\" \"A#4\" \"E5\") k) 0.12 (if (== k 2) 'down 'up) 1)))"
      "; 3. a polyrhythm: a against b in every two beats, four times (12-20)"
      "var a (head pr-of)"
      "var b (last pr-of)"
      "var pr (polyrhythm (tuplet a 2) (tuplet b 2))"
      "add-beats! s 12 (fragment-repeat (notes db 'Ob 'mf 'ord (take (list \"F5\" \"E5\" \"F#5\" \"D5\" \"G5\" \"C#5\" \"A5\") a) (head pr)) 4)"
      "add-beats! s 12 (fragment-repeat (notes db 'Hn 'mf 'ord (take (list \"C#3\" \"G3\" \"D3\" \"A2\" \"E3\" \"B2\" \"F3\") b) (last pr)) 4)"
      "; 4. an ostinato from a pattern (x an attack, . a continuation), then the same augmented (12-32)"
      "var ost (notes db 'Vc 'pp 'ord (list \"B3\" \"F3\") (rhythm-from-pattern \"x..x.x..\" 0.25))"
      "add-beats! s 12 (fragment-repeat ost 4)"
      "add-beats! s 20 (fragment-scale (fragment-repeat ost 3) 2)"
      "print a \"against\" b \": the oboe\" (join (map (head pr) (function (d) (fixed d 2))) \" \") \"beats, the horn\" (join (map (last pr) (function (d) (fixed d 2))) \" \")"
      "out 1 s"))
  (obj cuc comment "the score in Musil: walk, arpeggio, polyrhythm, rhythm-from-pattern" (pos 110 133))
  (obj sc score rhythms 2 @size 640 220 (pos 20 172))
  (obj tr transport 108 4 4 (pos 690 172))
  (obj sp message play (pos 690 207))
  (obj ss message stop (pos 735 207))
  (obj cpl comment "play / stop" (pos 785 208))
  (obj sum +~ (pos 20 417))
  (obj chall comment "the two channels summed, the volume ramped, then a hall (reverb~)" (pos 70 418))
  (obj half *~ 0.5 (pos 20 447))
  (obj lbv loadbang (pos 140 462))
  (obj vol message "0.8 300" (pos 140 492))
  (obj mute message "0 300" (pos 210 492))
  (obj cvol comment "volume up, down" (pos 270 493))
  (obj ramp line~ (pos 140 522))
  (obj vca *~ (pos 20 557))
  (obj rv reverb~ 0.25 2.5 (pos 20 587))
  (obj dac dac~ (pos 20 622))
  (connect dmic 0 c 1)
  (connect dful 0 c 1)
  (connect r1 0 c 0)
  (connect r2 0 c 0)
  (connect r3 0 c 0)
  (connect r4 0 c 0)
  (connect lb 0 r1 0)
  (connect c 0 sc 0)
  (connect sp 0 sc 0)
  (connect ss 0 sc 0)
  (connect sc 0 sum 0)
  (connect sc 1 sum 1)
  (connect sum 0 half 0)
  (connect half 0 vca 0)
  (connect lbv 0 vol 0)
  (connect vol 0 ramp 0)
  (connect mute 0 ramp 0)
  (connect ramp 0 vca 1)
  (connect vca 0 rv 0)
  (connect rv 0 dac 0)
  (connect rv 1 dac 1))
